WEBVTT

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.620
For the boat, it's Nard Lundy's town, let's keep it that way.

00:01:58.010 --> 00:01:58.670
Welcome to Boulder.

00:01:58.890 --> 00:01:59.410
Thank you, son.

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:01.540
Compromise to the mayor.

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:04.670
Now, why should the mayor give me three pocket chips?

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:06.590
Election time's coming in two weeks.

00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:09.630
Just the mayor's way of making sure you remember his name come voting time.

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:10.460
Vote?

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:11.650
Can't vote.

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:13.470
I don't even live here.

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:15.980
I just came here to see my daughter and her husband.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:16.660
Good.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:18.100
You've got family here.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.300
That's just the same as residents.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:20.780
Now, don't forget to vote.

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:21.720
It's Nard Lundy.

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:43.930
It's like I always figured, Jeff Rose is full of pickle juice.

00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:51.790
I'm Captain Orrin Hayes, late at the Texas Granges.

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:55.780
That man you just shot full of holes happens to be my son-in-law.

00:02:57.260 --> 00:02:59.360
You tell me where I can find his newspaper office?

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:02.300
Yeah, around the corner there to the right.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:18.640
Hey, why didn't you let us know you were coming?

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:20.420
Oh, I thought I'd surprise you.

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:21.960
I haven't seen you since you were married.

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:24.420
I've been retired from the Rangers now for some years.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:25.700
And he got lonesome.

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:27.470
Well, a man just can't quit.

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:29.420
Can't sit around.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:36.840
your arteries hardened i want some action travel help starve the blood but we're real happy to see

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:43.200
you and you stay as long as you please thank you thank you say looks like you've got quite a

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:51.230
business going here but uh tell me something son what are those wanted posters on you around town

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:56.910
those aren't wanted posters papa those are campaign posters jeff is a candidate for mayor

00:03:56.910 --> 00:03:59.890
well the way they're shooting his picture full of holes

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:05.540
i'd say you're not wanted mayor lundie's a very clever opponent captain owns most of this town

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:19.840
and runs it from his hel dorado saloon my dear lovely as always well how are you

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:31.940
I'll come in on the stage a couple of minutes ago, Mayor.

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:33.220
Old fellow.

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:35.520
Says he used to be with the Texas Rangers.

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:38.580
And Jeff Rose is his son-in-law.

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:42.600
Well, if he's old, he shouldn't worry you, Clyde.

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:46.180
And if he doesn't live here, he can't vote for Jeff, so he doesn't worry me.

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:49.000
Nard, have you seen this new edition of the Sentinel?

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:52.370
He's got your whole record in there.

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:53.450
Mine, too.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:55.640
Yours, too, Clyde.

00:04:56.170 --> 00:04:59.910
All the facts and figures, the dates, all the graphs.

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:05.820
The payoffs, all the illegal taxes, but he says I ain't a proper judge.

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:10.490
He says I'm guilty of malfeasance, whatever that is.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:17.170
Means you are a walking whiskey vat and you bought your Justice of the Peace office years ago from Charlie Reeves.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:19.440
But I've still got my office.

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:22.880
Only because I keep you there, don't forget that, Your Honor.

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:29.960
Now don't you just cut out Amos, you know, a smart man who's handy with...

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:36.040
Tough opponent. When he starts to smear you with the truth, he is deadly.

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:39.820
If this paper ever gets to the governor's office...

00:05:40.030 --> 00:05:44.140
Get the boys all together. Round up. Every copy of this is in circulation.

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:46.420
Buy him, steal him, take him, but get him.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:52.300
Tell him you're all along, Nard. You give that newspaper fellow too much rope.

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:56.590
You always got things done right. Oh, no, no, no, no.

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:59.920
I'm not the sort of man to use force.

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:02.240
when gentle persuasion will serve.

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:05.020
Why don't you get your deputies together

00:06:05.020 --> 00:06:07.640
and pay yourself a little call, Mr. Rose?

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:17.100
Sure rake this Lundy over the cold.

00:06:18.530 --> 00:06:20.670
Well, if it's a battle he wants, let's give it to him.

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:22.230
I'll pitch in and help.

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:23.300
Do me good.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:25.240
A little action is what I need.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.810
You here on law business, Sheriff?

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:36.160
No, we're just a bunch of plain citizens.

00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:42.010
Come to tell you that we don't hold with your brand a mud-slinging, name-calling politics.

00:06:43.890 --> 00:06:45.350
We don't want you printing nothing more.

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:46.620
Nothing.

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:47.860
Now, wait a minute, Sheriff.

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:50.450
You can't interfere with the freedom of the press.

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:52.640
Keep out of this, you Morsehorn.

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:54.010
Morsehorn?

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:55.700
Listen, young fella.

00:06:56.550 --> 00:06:59.550
On your best day, you couldn't curry mules in my outfit.

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:00.780
Thank you.

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:47.140
Get out of here.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.770
Jeff, you've got to give up.

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:03.750
Lenny's too powerful. He's too dangerous.

00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:06.520
Maybe next time you'll order Sheriff Barnes to use his gun.

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:09.220
That's exactly why he's got to be fought and beaten.

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:12.500
Yeah, the best thing for you to do is strap on your own gun

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:13.420
and fight him in his way.

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:16.000
Captain Hayes, I know gunplay was necessary

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:17.840
in the days when you were with the Texas Rangers,

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:20.370
but if we're ever going to have progress in the West,

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:23.350
we've got to learn to fight our battles with ideas and words.

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:25.890
Well, it looks like you can't run out of words.

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:29.970
Maybe Hannah's right. Maybe I should give up.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:33.250
You know, a lot of people were glad to see me run against Lundy,

00:08:33.350 --> 00:08:34.830
but none of them would lift a finger to help.

00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:38.290
I know a handful of men, just three,

00:08:39.220 --> 00:08:41.480
who could straighten out Lundy and his gang in a hurry.

00:08:42.230 --> 00:08:42.870
Who's that, Captain?

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:48.260
Fastest guns in the West, finest riders, top scouts,

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:51.420
crack men who served with me on the Ripper process,

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:56.140
brought law and order to the Lone Star State,

00:08:57.400 --> 00:08:59.120
pride of the Texas Rangers.

00:09:01.690 --> 00:09:05.130
First off, I'll send to Abilene for Nash Crawford.

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:07.880
His gun was quicker than the blink of a cougar,

00:09:08.350 --> 00:09:10.550
faster than the flick of a prairie dog's tail.

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:14.200
Be a gun, mister, and you'll be dead before it kills later.

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:24.720
Boss, is that exactly the way you had to shoot out with Sam Bass?

00:09:24.890 --> 00:09:26.930
Well, of course, the Sloan won't all cluttered up

00:09:26.930 --> 00:09:29.030
with degars and dinguses like this.

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:29.960
Now you've...

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.380
Let's clean this up for you more season.

00:09:31.780 --> 00:09:35.200
And this is trading the Rangers.

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:36.630
What's your grandpa?

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:40.210
Well, it's a much smaller than McCall 45, more like a hideout gun.

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:41.780
What's a hideout gun?

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:44.310
Well, come on over here and I'll tell you about it.

00:09:48.030 --> 00:09:48.590
Take yourself down.

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:55.230
Now, I recall I was wintering in the bend on the San Sabo River, east of that eye building, see?

00:09:56.130 --> 00:09:59.450
The captain sent me on a scout after a fellow who was wanted for murdering a horse thieving.

00:10:00.380 --> 00:10:04.080
Well, boys, that's when I got my first taste of a hideout gun.

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:05.000
You see?

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:07.580
What was that crash I heard in here a minute ago?

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:09.280
Oh, my fault, Ellie.

00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:10.640
Had a little accident with a lamp.

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:16.040
I suppose the Texas Rangers just won another battle against overwhelming odds?

00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:19.200
Run along, boys.

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:20.020
It's time for your nap.

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:23.880
Oh, Grandpa, he's gonna kill us again.

00:10:24.940 --> 00:10:25.800
Like your ma says.

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:35.940
you don't mean any harm but you've got to stop filling the boys head full of those blood-curdling

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:44.390
fairy tales about fighting horse thieves indians fairy tales well them things really happen fact

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:54.430
is i even told the kids the bloodiest ones here next i'll send to kansas city for jason fitch

00:10:55.060 --> 00:10:59.970
second best man with a gun and the finest scout in the rangers he has eyes like a haw

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:07.830
in the daytime eyes like an owl at night captain right after them two fellers i know they're a mile

00:11:07.830 --> 00:11:18.450
off but i can tell they're comanches big one's a chief tail with a mark on his forehead tip of

00:11:18.450 --> 00:11:23.370
a feather sticking up behind a boulder way off there to the south feather of a scissor tail of

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:26.470
flycatcher. Another Comanche beneath it.

00:11:33.740 --> 00:11:40.270
You must have been a marvelous scout, Mr. Fitch, to recognize all those terrible Indians so far away.

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:43.000
Takes eyes like an eagle, Mrs. Fletcher.

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:45.520
I'm Mrs. Murphy.

00:11:49.510 --> 00:11:51.880
You're Mrs. Murphy, not Mrs. Fletcher.

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:55.150
Hey, you're a pretty little thing.

00:11:55.690 --> 00:11:59.410
Mr. Fitch, you're really much too bold at times.

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:02.880
Once I had a shootout with three dudes over a woman like you.

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:04.320
Mr. Fitch.

00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:06.340
Real catalog woman she was.

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:07.470
Great little thing.

00:12:08.220 --> 00:12:09.140
Just like you.

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:09.740
Mr.

00:12:11.560 --> 00:12:12.920
Mr. Fitch, Mr. Fitch.

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:14.410
Find your own woman, boy.

00:12:14.890 --> 00:12:16.750
This telegram just came for you.

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:18.510
Somebody's dead.

00:12:20.140 --> 00:12:21.480
You don't have a black border.

00:12:21.860 --> 00:12:22.460
Let's see it.

00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:27.360
You tell me what that says, Ms. Murphy.

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:29.740
I need my strong glasses for reading.

00:12:30.760 --> 00:12:32.580
It says, Brazos.

00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:37.800
The old cold word of our company means trouble.

00:12:38.100 --> 00:12:39.620
Strap on your gun and hit the trail.

00:12:40.310 --> 00:12:41.250
What else does it say?

00:12:41.750 --> 00:12:43.090
It's just an address.

00:12:43.930 --> 00:12:48.610
Sully's mine on Feather Wash, south of Boulder, Nevada.

00:12:49.260 --> 00:12:51.360
Signed, Captain Orrin Hayes.

00:12:51.490 --> 00:12:52.550
Captain Orrin Hayes.

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:54.070
Our old outfits back in action.

00:12:54.340 --> 00:12:55.840
I gotta line out for Nevada fast.

00:12:56.280 --> 00:12:58.160
We'll help you get packed, Mr. Fitch.

00:13:04.190 --> 00:13:05.550
How can I help Captain Hayes?

00:13:06.290 --> 00:13:07.930
Don't you feel up to it?

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:10.580
Sure I feel up to it and over it and way past it.

00:13:11.510 --> 00:13:13.150
A man is a long way from Kansas City.

00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:16.890
I haven't got no horse or artillery.

00:13:17.540 --> 00:13:18.980
No money to make a trip if I did.

00:13:28.310 --> 00:13:29.680
I feel up for Captain and think I'm dead.

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:33.020
Maybe we ought to be.

00:14:05.920 --> 00:14:07.880
Boy, I just delivered a telegram for you.

00:14:09.460 --> 00:14:11.700
Oh, Johnny, you sent me a telegram.

00:14:15.590 --> 00:14:16.170
Say, Pa.

00:14:17.300 --> 00:14:17.780
Brazos!

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:20.160
That's all? Brazos?

00:14:20.530 --> 00:14:22.210
No, there's an address here, too.

00:14:22.910 --> 00:14:26.030
Sally's Mine on Feather Wash, south of Boulder, Nevada.

00:14:27.430 --> 00:14:29.070
And it's signed Captain Orrin Hayes.

00:14:29.460 --> 00:14:29.960
My old Cap...

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:31.280
I'm Captain from Texas Rangers, Ellie.

00:14:31.730 --> 00:14:33.820
He's calling me to ride again.

00:14:34.780 --> 00:14:35.710
Troubles? Shooting?

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:39.010
Brazos! The old code word.

00:14:39.320 --> 00:14:40.680
They always used to call us together.

00:14:42.680 --> 00:14:44.280
Well, it's a kind of reunion.

00:14:49.560 --> 00:14:51.440
You've heard from Captain Hayes and...

00:14:51.590 --> 00:14:54.990
Ellie, come a-running when he hears that word, Brazos.

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:57.960
You're out, it's all good enough. It's spread over the whole country.

00:15:00.800 --> 00:15:02.540
No ranger retired perpendicular.

00:15:04.890 --> 00:15:06.550
Well, it's an awful long wait in Nevada.

00:15:07.110 --> 00:15:09.690
Yeah, well, it was a far piece down in the Oasis,

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:12.840
past Fort Clark, and up the Devil's River,

00:15:13.900 --> 00:15:14.880
and on the Beaver Lake.

00:15:15.190 --> 00:15:17.450
They hit the kicker post, but we made it.

00:15:18.360 --> 00:15:20.300
How were you going to eat and sleep along the way?

00:15:20.780 --> 00:15:21.980
What were you going to do for money?

00:15:22.740 --> 00:15:23.560
Oh, I've saved a little.

00:15:24.240 --> 00:15:24.780
From what?

00:15:26.170 --> 00:15:27.150
From not spending it.

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:35.430
If your mind's made up, then I guess I can only kiss you goodbye and wish you good luck.

00:15:37.930 --> 00:15:38.510
Yes, sir?

00:15:39.590 --> 00:15:40.950
Can you throw this gear on the horse?

00:15:41.190 --> 00:15:41.610
Pa!

00:15:42.230 --> 00:15:42.510
What?

00:15:43.090 --> 00:15:44.130
We don't own a horse.

00:15:48.050 --> 00:15:51.180
Not least, I'll send for a gentleman, George Agnew.

00:15:52.180 --> 00:15:57.300
Call him gentleman because of his spotless character, his courtly manners, his fit and polished appearance.

00:16:09.050 --> 00:16:14.060
Now, I'm telling you, gentlemen, George, you stay out of this saloon for good.

00:16:14.460 --> 00:16:17.160
Doggone, Mac, I'm going to miss going in that saloon of yours.

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:20.630
You know what? I get to liking a man. I freeze.

00:16:21.860 --> 00:16:23.500
I'm freezing you out.

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:29.720
Now, there's your car. And don't try using that slippery deck again.

00:16:30.510 --> 00:16:32.510
Next place, you're liable to wind up full of holes.

00:16:41.470 --> 00:16:46.050
So they caught you pulling a little flim-flam and jiggery-pokery with the cards again, huh, George?

00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:49.980
Sure, if I just filled out an inside straight, fair and square.

00:16:50.580 --> 00:16:54.580
I could have used this ace, but the deuces wasn't wild.

00:16:54.900 --> 00:16:57.280
No, Mac didn't throw you out just for the exercise.

00:16:58.240 --> 00:16:59.820
That joke was on Mac.

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:08.240
did was reach in my pistol pocket for my harmonica yeah i'll play you a little piece but i i think you

00:17:08.240 --> 00:17:13.300
best move on out of range now why don't you go on home and get some sleep i ain't got no room frank

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:19.800
i've been doing all my sleeping in max saloon in yonder oh i didn't need a bed i could toss you in

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:28.540
jail what for most anything for inciting a riot for for littering up the streets now come on i

00:17:28.540 --> 00:17:29.760
I want to put you all that bother.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:32.500
I'll just find myself at the saloon.

00:17:32.840 --> 00:17:36.760
George, you have used up every saloon in the whole Oklahoma Territory.

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:39.790
Well, there must be somebody building a new one around here somewhere.

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:42.220
George, George Agnew.

00:17:42.520 --> 00:17:42.860
No!

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:47.310
I got a telegram for you, George.

00:17:47.910 --> 00:17:50.110
No world would be sending me a telegram.

00:17:51.260 --> 00:17:59.190
See, just send me.

00:17:59.430 --> 00:17:59.950
I'm warned.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:02.600
Well, that don't surprise me none. Who buy?

00:18:02.780 --> 00:18:03.800
The Texas Rangers.

00:18:04.450 --> 00:18:06.930
My old captain wants me to come up the divider.

00:18:07.360 --> 00:18:10.540
You know how I gotta get me a broom-tailed fiddle-footer and ride.

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:39.270
Why, you long-legged, you necked broom-tailed.

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:42.160
It's the first time I've ever seen one jackass riding another.

00:18:42.500 --> 00:18:44.200
Now, who you calling a jackass?

00:18:44.730 --> 00:18:47.950
You old moss-backed, bull-winded, kettle-bellied...

00:18:47.950 --> 00:18:48.410
George!

00:18:48.940 --> 00:18:49.400
Nash!

00:18:51.510 --> 00:18:53.870
Good to see you.

00:18:53.990 --> 00:18:55.050
Good to see you again.

00:18:55.350 --> 00:18:56.830
Did you answer the captain's call?

00:18:57.090 --> 00:18:59.980
Yep, thinking he had real need of good fighting, man.

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:02.900
But I don't know, seeing as how he called on you.

00:19:03.390 --> 00:19:04.470
You old coot.

00:19:05.060 --> 00:19:08.040
Who got them two cattle rustlers down in Bandera County that time?

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:08.720
I did.

00:19:08.840 --> 00:19:09.980
I winged them for you.

00:19:11.980 --> 00:19:13.480
George, you're looking a little poorly.

00:19:14.450 --> 00:19:16.130
Kind of scummy and going to grass belly.

00:19:17.790 --> 00:19:19.270
Fuck, you weren't too good yourself.

00:19:19.660 --> 00:19:21.020
And who left you up on that horse?

00:19:21.430 --> 00:19:23.490
You must be 95 if you were a day.

00:19:23.820 --> 00:19:25.780
Well, I reckon my gun ain't aged none.

00:19:26.380 --> 00:19:28.430
I reckon that's what counts, Sergeant.

00:19:28.820 --> 00:19:29.460
Then let's ride.

00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:59.620
Your dang know you're a cypressorite.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:02.030
You or I must be mighty sure, Jase.

00:20:02.490 --> 00:20:03.610
I'm Nash Crawford.

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:06.980
Oh, sure, I'd know you anywhere, Nash.

00:20:07.330 --> 00:20:09.360
Red hair, straight as a ramrod,

00:20:09.700 --> 00:20:10.980
skinny waist like a girl's.

00:20:11.240 --> 00:20:13.320
Well, by jingles, the captain sure called up

